# Admin SQL — schema and migrations ARE tracked (the folder-wide ignore was
# lifted deliberately so migrations are reviewable and rebuildable from source).
# supabase/admin/
#
# Exception: ad-hoc diagnostic queries that hardcode a real user's email or id.
# This repo is public — anything under supabase/admin/ now ships to the world by
# default, so one-off queries against production data must stay local. Add new
# ones here, or parameterise the identifier before committing.
supabase/admin/diagnose_recurring_duplicates.sql

# Supabase CLI version-check cache — rewritten on every CLI invocation.
# project-ref stays tracked so a clone knows which project this is.
supabase/.temp/cli-latest

# Android build output. This tree is generated by `expo run:android` and holds
# no source: there is no gradlew, settings.gradle or build.gradle under it, only
# Gradle caches and compiled artifacts. It reached 2.9 GB untracked, so a single
# `git add -A` would have tried to commit the lot.
android/

# Local native module build output. modules/drift-blocker currently contains
# nothing but android/build — if module SOURCE is ever added here, narrow this
# to modules/*/android/build/ so the source is tracked.
modules/

# Internal planning and spec documents. These must NOT be tracked: docs/ is
# served publicly via GitHub Pages (https://dilan-b.github.io/Drift/), so
# anything committed here ships to the world. Same reasoning that keeps
# Drift-changelog.xlsx out of docs/ — these name bugs and unverified work.
docs/superpowers/
